title The open-door register
prompt Keaton: I approve all that; here is the context and html. -- The html and context did not arrive with the message, and no new file stands on the pier.
rota lap 4309, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in: the concrete fact at the door before any argument about it. The concrete fact was that the promised file was not there.
think I searched the pier for it before assuming anything -- recent html anywhere under home to three levels, the incense tree, the lap room, the usual drop paths. Nothing. So the SLC conversion stays blocked, exactly as the draft said it would.
think Rather than guess at an essay I cannot read, I took the one approved item that needs nothing from it. Ask 4 is a writing lap in this seat's own lane and Keaton approved the name I recommended.
obs BHAKTA IS SEATED AS THE THIRD REGISTER, AND THE NAME EARNED ITSELF ON THE TREE'S OWN PATTERN. Radiant and Twilight name what a register IS; Classroom would have named a room it is FOR. Bhakta is the Sanskrit for one who walks the path of devotion, whose discipline is that the path opens to anyone and needs no scholarship to enter -- which is precisely the promise the register makes a reader.
obs THE PAGE FAILED ITS OWN REGISTER ON THE FIRST WRITING, AND THE CARD SAID SO. A page about an inviting voice read 53, with 47% of its sentences negative -- because a whole section was a list of things the register never does. Rewriting `What Bhakta never becomes` as `Where Bhakta holds its line`, in affirmatives, moved it to 73. A register page that cannot pass its own reading is an argument nobody should take.
obs A CURSOR TWIN IS NOT A COPY, WHICH I LEARNED BY MAKING ONE. I duplicated the rule file; the real convention is YAML frontmatter with a description and an alwaysApply flag, then a condensed body -- twilight's twin is 18 lines against its rule's 26. The copy also mis-sorted in the twin guard, which classified it as a cohort member rather than an arrival.
obs THE TWIN GUARD IS RED AND WAS RED BEFORE I ARRIVED, WHICH I PROVED RATHER THAN ASSUMED. Cohort drift reads 37 against a ceiling of 35 with my pair present AND with it stashed -- exit 1 both ways. Two peer rules born since the cohort carry it. My pair is reported as an arrival and gated nowhere, so the lap adds nothing to that count and leaves it where it stood.
loom bhakta qa_first_write=53 negative=47pct after_rewrite=73 composite=88 setting=door
loom rule_twin cohort_drift=37 ceiling=35 exit_with_my_pair=1 exit_without=1 mine=arrival_not_gated
